# Build context for the notifier image (docker-compose builds ./pipeline).
#
# A .dockerignore applies to the root of its own build context, so the repo-root
# one does not cover this directory — hence a second file.
#
# Most importantly: dogwatch-notify.config.json holds RTSP/NVR credentials and
# the Telegram chat id. It is gitignored, but it lives right here on the
# deployment host and would otherwise be uploaded into the build context on
# every build. The real config is bind-mounted at runtime; only the .example is
# ever needed at build time (and even that isn't COPYed).
dogwatch-notify.config.json
*.state
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.md
